503
00:21:26.352 --> 00:21:28.165
I to C: how did he react.

504
00:21:28.445 --> 00:21:32.200
C to I: his point about refunds became part of the design.

505
00:21:32.480 --> 00:21:35.147
I to C: what if the review had gone the other way.

506
00:21:35.427 --> 00:21:39.352
C to I: commit, record the revisit metric, make projection cheap.

507
00:21:39.632 --> 00:21:41.723
I to C: what would you do differently.

508
00:21:42.003 --> 00:21:44.776
C to I: bring the product manager in earlier.

509
00:21:45.056 --> 00:21:49.707
I to I: scores - scope B3, influence B3, self-awareness strong.

510
00:21:53.557 --> 00:21:55.775
Sequence: a vague story under probing.

511
00:21:56.055 --> 00:21:58.850
The sequence diagram walks through it step by step.

512
00:21:59.130 --> 00:22:01.221
I to C: tell me about a failure.

513
00:22:01.501 --> 00:22:05.533
C to I: we migrated search, relevance was worse, we rolled back.

514
00:22:05.813 --> 00:22:07.605
I to C: what was your role.

515
00:22:07.885 --> 00:22:08.781
C to I:

516
00:22:09.061 --> 00:22:10.213
I was on the team.

517
00:22:10.493 --> 00:22:13.735
I to C: what did you personally do differently afterwards.

518
00:22:14.015 --> 00:22:16.447
C to I: we test more languages now.

519
00:22:16.727 --> 00:22:19.095
I to C: how did you measure the impact.

520
00:22:19.375 --> 00:22:20.869
C to I: not sure.

521
00:22:21.149 --> 00:22:24.903
I to I: scores - ownership unclear, no evidence, below level.

522
00:22:28.753 --> 00:22:30.567
State: a story's lifecycle.

523
00:22:30.847 --> 00:22:32.191
Here is the diagram.

